  "id": "COMPOUND:3454 - PROTEIN:6081",
  "verbalization": "Digoxigenin appears to have a potential mechanism of action involving the Taste receptor type 2 member 31 through multiple interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Digoxigenin targets SK-HEP1 cells, which are then targeted by Protobioside and 8-Prenylluteone, both of which ultimately interact with the Taste receptor type 2 member 31. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Digoxigenin may modulate the activity of the receptor through its interaction with downstream targets. The presence of multiple independent pathways linking Digoxigenin to the receptor suggests a plausible, though not yet fully elucidated, mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network and underscores the need for further investigation into the specific molecular interactions that govern this relationship.",
